<section class="vt-casestudy"><div class="vt-casestudy__inner"><div class="vt-casestudy__img-col"><div class="vt-casestudy__img-wrap"><img src="/images/vista-window-film-philadelphia-casestudy.jpg" alt="University City medical center with Vista window film on west-facing patient room glass" title="Vista window film Philadelphia healthcare case study" width="1264" height="848" loading="lazy" class="vt-casestudy__img" /><div class="vt-casestudy__badge"><span class="vt-casestudy__badge-label">Vista Case Study</span></div></div></div><div class="vt-casestudy__content"><span class="pp-eyebrow">Case Study</span><h2 class="vt-casestudy__title">How Vista SpectraSelect Solved a Philadelphia Healthcare Facility's Glass Problem</h2><p class="vt-casestudy__body">A University City healthcare facility with significant west-facing patient room glazing contracted Window Film Philadelphia to install Vista SpectraSelect. The project required NFRC-certified documentation for institutional procurement, careful phasing to keep patient rooms operational, and a product that satisfied both the facilities team and the design review process.</p><blockquote class="vt-casestudy__quote"><p>&ldquo;The patient rooms facing west had been a comfort complaint for years. After Vista SpectraSelect, the rooms are noticeably more comfortable and the staff reports patients sleeping better on afternoon shifts.&rdquo;</p><footer>Facilities Manager, University City Medical Center</footer></blockquote></div></div></section>

